  "theorem": "Ampas.Claims.el_comm_independent",
  "text": "The monoid axioms do not derive commutativity in equational logic, and adding commutativity does not trivialize the theory: x = y remains underivable. (Not \"inconsistent\": a pure equational theory always has a one-element model, so inconsistency in the usual sense is unreachable. The degenerate case the second conjunct excludes is trivialization -- every equation becoming derivable, which substitution would give from x = y.)",
